            <ArticleTitle>Tophaceous gout of the axial skeleton.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>865-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 72-year-old female with a recent episode of podagra, without peripheral tophi, presented with nocturnal back pain and a destructive lesion of the right lamina of L4. A tophus was excised at laminectomy. Evidence of an axial skeletal tophus causing an irritative radiculopathy via mass effect is presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
